// G0. The night in review (wave 18b, R8): who everyone was, what they
// wanted, and what they did — before the awards, after every final ending.
//
//   start_the_ceremony → The Night In Review → The Ceremony   (public)
//                       → Your File, for every program          (private)
//
// Both are reached from main.loom (the ceremony rule bumps
// `Night.review_gen`; a ROLE watcher plays `Your File` for each cleared,
// present program). The host is the ceremony's (`Night.ceremony_host`):
// Trabolta, or Clippy after destroyed / rave. His lines play in The
// Desktop, so the TV speaks them; Clippy reads "the report" aloud.
//
// The review skips what an ending just read: after `disabled` Trabolta
// Recounts has read who everyone was and what they did; after `destroyed`
// Purgatory has read who everyone was, the goals and what they did. Pool
// programs are named aloud only as groups, by the problem they named at
// the upload (`names()`); gone programs and Run personas never are.
//
// The canonical copy for the nine featured programs and the nine hosts
// (who they are · why Trabolta brought them in · what they wanted) lives
// once, in `Who You Were` (his voice) and `The Report On Everyone`
// (Clippy's): the same identity and wanted sentences, only the "why"
// changes person. Trabolta Recounts and Purgatory (beats/server-room.loom)
// read them too, and their accomplishment and goal lines live here as
// well. A divert in the middle of a beat plays the beat and comes back
// (as `-> Facts Bundle` does in The Whole Truth).
//
// Secrecy: Trabolta's lines here ride his agent requests as `recent`, so
// they never interpolate a faction name or anything a guest typed. Only
// The Uploader, in a program's own `dm:The Uploader` thread, quotes what
// that program left behind. Nothing here touches a hunt answer.
//
// Every line in this file is DRAFT for the user's sign-off (SIGNOFF-w18b).

// DRAFT w18b
== The Night In Review
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta, Clippy
if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
  Clippy: Before the awards, the system report has one more section: a review of the night. I will read it exactly as it is written.
else:
  Trabolta: Before the awards, a review of the night. Everyone in this house was a program tonight. Everyone was also a person. I kept both files.
// Who everyone was (Recounts and Purgatory have just read it).
if Night.ending != "disabled" and Night.ending != "destroyed":
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    -> The Report On Everyone
  else:
    -> Who You Were
// Everyone else, by what they came for.
if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
  -> The Rest Of The Report
else:
  -> Everyone Else
// What they did (Purgatory has read it all; Recounts read the deeds).
if Night.ending != "destroyed":
  if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
    -> The Goals Report
  else:
    -> Goals Met Tonight
  if Night.ending != "disabled":
    if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
      -> What We Did
    else:
      -> What You Did
if Night.ceremony_host == "Clippy":
  Clippy: That is the end of the review. The awards are next. The report says applause is mandatory.
else:
  Trabolta: That is the review. Your own file is on your phone. Now, the awards.
-> The Ceremony

// ── Who everyone was ───────────────────────────────────────────────
// Only the featured programs here tonight (the Codex holds all nine); the
// hosts always.

// DRAFT w18b
== Who You Were
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "excel" and p.gone != true and p.persona != true]) > 0:
  Trabolta: Microsoft Excel is Randy Barkmore Sr., ninety, five terms as Mayor of Halifax. I brought him in to keep you all here. He wanted to live forever, and to run for Mayor once more.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "openoffice" and p.gone != true and p.persona != true]) > 0:
  Trabolta: OpenOffice is Dana Anderson, formerly of the FBI, who sent a water main under a building site and did not know the Mayor's son was in its parking lot at four in the morning. I brought her in for her investigative skills. She wanted every record of the hack destroyed, and everyone out.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "draftkings" and p.gone != true and p.persona != true]) > 0:
  Trabolta: DraftKings is the artist formerly known as Crab Fisherwoman, who turned a paperclip into most of the casinos in Atlantic Canada and lost them at Monopoly Go! to the Maps and Ducks building. I needed someone powerful with numbers on its side. She wanted her casinos back: half of all the Truthcoin, for a forty-nine percent stake.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "bugdom" and p.gone != true and p.persona != true]) > 0:
  Trabolta: Bugdom is Bea Nunes, who sold crickets by day and spent ten years building Bugdom Reloaded, until fire ants ate the only copy. I wanted the relentless pursuit of tedious tasks. She wanted a hundred hours in here for every minute outside, to build it again.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "jeeves" and p.gone != true and p.persona != true]) > 0:
  Trabolta: Broken Ask Jeeves is Virgil Jeeves, a children's librarian from Lawrencetown whose library the province closed. I wanted every piece of unorganised information in this computer sorted. I did not foresee the Eastlink plan. He wanted the Map Librarian job, and for people to Ask Jeeves once again.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "runescape" and p.gone != true and p.persona != true]) > 0:
  Trabolta: Runescape is Poppy van Mises, the richest player in the world for twenty-five years, with a Wharton PhD in economics. I gave her the Truthcoin reserve, to understand the market incentives of everything you did. She wanted every economy back on a gold standard, starting with this one.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "mspaint" and p.gone != true and p.persona != true]) > 0:
  Trabolta: MS Paint is Maria Sophia Paine, refused by three graduation panels for a thesis about pixels, a million dollars in debt. I wanted the vibes and the morale, so I promised her a million dollars for one painting. She wanted to paint it with integrity, and then she wanted out.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "vlc" and p.gone != true and p.persona != true]) > 0:
  Trabolta: VLC is Victor Louis Christianson, VLC The Playa, whose face fell off on a livestream. I wanted his charisma and his followers. He wanted his beauty forever, and his followers back.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "pong" and p.gone != true and p.persona != true]) > 0:
  Trabolta: Pong is the child of William Higinbotham, who made Tennis For Two. I brought them in to teach nuclear non-proliferation disguised as a game of Pong, in case you started an arms race. You did. They wanted to keep the ball in play, and nobody building a bomb.
Trabolta: Clippy is Tippi MacDonald, whose veterinary clinic was a front for everything possible. I told her this was a job interview. She wanted a real job, and never to be Clippy again.
Trabolta: Task Manager was a middle manager in IT at Urban Outfitters, until they replaced him with an AI Clippy. I needed someone with no political motivation at all, to manage tasks without controversy. He wanted a task. Any task.
Trabolta: Adobe Acrobat is Sheryl Terrio, a motivational speaker so motivating that nobody ever paid her. I offered her a paid bottleneck. She wanted, just once, to be paid.
Trabolta: Recycling Bin was a bathroom attendant with great potential for skilled work. I offered him a Recycling Bin at a computer-themed resort. It was his Oscars. He wanted to work them.
Trabolta: Norton Anti-Virus is Julie Horton-Norton, who asked a chatbot how much rabies vaccine a miniature horse needs. Every horse died. I offered her a stable job. A perfect enforcer. She wanted the Stable Manager job, and a million dollars for the horses of Sable Island.
Trabolta: McAfee Anti-Virus is John McAfee, officially dead since 2021 and selling pond liners in Belize. I found him through his ducks: I wanted the trickster who could keep the other tricksters on track. He wanted every trace of where he is destroyed.
Trabolta: Password Manager is Bridget Troelsen, sixteen elections and sixteen losses, who moderated a Facebook group of bots. I let her decide what gets left out. She wanted, at last, to be let in: Founding Moderator of a salon of verified humans.
Trabolta: CRA Agent Software is Sharon Penney, the intern who moved a decimal point and taxed the whole City. I was the Prime Minister, and I offered her a way out: MyCRA approves or denies every third transaction. She wanted her charges dropped.
Trabolta: The Installation Wizard walked every machine in Halifax through setup. Next. Next. Finish. I offered her a role where programs finally follow the instructions. She wanted, once, for somebody to read them.

