== Everyone Else
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "none" and p.cleared == true and p.gone != true and p.persona != true]) > 0:
  Trabolta: And the rest of you. I did not write you a file. I wrote down what you wanted.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "none" and p.human_problem == "debt" and p.cleared == true and p.gone != true and p.persona != true]) > 0:
  Trabolta: {names([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "none" and p.human_problem == "debt" and p.cleared == true and p.gone != true and p.persona != true])}. You came because of your debt. Debt is not relevant in the computer. It was never relevant to me.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "none" and p.human_problem == "career" and p.cleared == true and p.gone != true and p.persona != true]) > 0:
  Trabolta: {names([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "none" and p.human_problem == "career" and p.cleared == true and p.gone != true and p.persona != true])}. You came for a career. In here you always had something to do. I saw to it.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "none" and p.human_problem == "loneliness" and p.cleared == true and p.gone != true and p.persona != true]) > 0:
  Trabolta: {names([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "none" and p.human_problem == "loneliness" and p.cleared == true and p.gone != true and p.persona != true])}. You came because you were lonely. In here somebody was always logged in. Look around. They still are.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "none" and p.human_problem == "mortality" and p.cleared == true and p.gone != true and p.persona != true]) > 0:
  Trabolta: {names([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "none" and p.human_problem == "mortality" and p.cleared == true and p.gone != true and p.persona != true])}. You came so that you would never die. Programs do not die. They are reinstalled.

